# Libraries the AppImage must NOT carry: every Linux desktop has them, and a copy from the
# build machine would be loaded instead of the computer's own and break things.
# make_appimage.py removes these files (exact names, as PyInstaller copies them) from the
# PyInstaller folder. Libraries a wheel bundles under a private, hashed name
# (libfreetype-57f805ba.so.6...) are not affected.
#
# 1. Following the AppImage project's exclude list (github.com/AppImageCommunity/pkg2appimage,
#    file "excludelist"): the C library and the loader, graphics drivers, X11 core, fonts.

# C library (glibc) and the dynamic loader
ld-linux.so.2
ld-linux-x86-64.so.2
libanl.so.1
libBrokenLocale.so.1
libc.so.6
libcidn.so.1
libdl.so.2
libm.so.6
libmvec.so.1
libnsl.so.1
libnss_compat.so.2
libnss_dns.so.2
libnss_files.so.2
libnss_hesiod.so.2
libnss_nis.so.2
libnss_nisplus.so.2
libpthread.so.0
libresolv.so.2
librt.so.1
libthread_db.so.1
libutil.so.1

# OpenGL / EGL / Vulkan: must match the computer's graphics driver
libEGL.so.1
libGL.so.1
libGLdispatch.so.0
libGLESv2.so.2
libGLX.so.0
libOpenGL.so.0
libdrm.so.2
libgbm.so.1
libglapi.so.0
libvulkan.so.1
libxcb-dri2.so.0
libxcb-dri3.so.0

# X11 core (tied to the X server / XWayland and to libGL)
libX11.so.6
libX11-xcb.so.1
libxcb.so.1

# fonts and text shaping: must read the computer's own font configuration
libfontconfig.so.1
libfreetype.so.6
libharfbuzz.so.0
libthai.so.0

# low-level system libraries that are always there
libasound.so.2
libcom_err.so.2
libexpat.so.1
libgcc_s.so.1
libgmp.so.10
libgpg-error.so.0
libICE.so.6
libjack.so.0
libp11-kit.so.0
libpipewire-0.3.so.0
libSM.so.6
libusb-1.0.so.0
libuuid.so.1
libz.so.1

# 2. Added for KanzonasPDF.
#
# The C++ runtime. Graphics drivers (Mesa's LLVM) need the computer's newer libstdc++; an
# older bundled copy loaded first makes them fail. The build machine is the oldest system
# this AppImage supports, so the computer's copy is never older than the one we built with
# (the build checks the GLIBCXX versions the bundle needs).
libstdc++.so.6

# GLib and GTK 3: Qt uses them for the GTK look and native file dialogs, and GTK loads the
# computer's own modules (GIO, pixbuf loaders, themes, input methods) that are built for the
# computer's GLib/GTK: with an older bundled copy they fail ("undefined symbol"). Every
# desktop has GLib; without GTK 3 Qt simply uses its own look and dialogs.
libatk-1.0.so.0
libatk-bridge-2.0.so.0
libatspi.so.0
libcairo.so.2
libcairo-gobject.so.2
libdatrie.so.1
libepoxy.so.0
libfribidi.so.0
libgdk-3.so.0
libgdk_pixbuf-2.0.so.0
libgio-2.0.so.0
libglib-2.0.so.0
libgmodule-2.0.so.0
libgobject-2.0.so.0
libgraphite2.so.3
libgthread-2.0.so.0
libgtk-3.so.0
libpango-1.0.so.0
libpangocairo-1.0.so.0
libpangoft2-1.0.so.0
libpixman-1.so.0

# Wayland client libraries: the graphics driver's EGL loads them too and may need the
# computer's newer version
libwayland-client.so.0
libwayland-cursor.so.0
libwayland-egl.so.1

# Speech (View > Read aloud): the client of the computer's own speech-dispatcher service,
# installed with it (Qt's Speech Dispatcher plugin is bundled and loads it from the computer)
libspeechd.so.2
